    /// particular Services and/or Systems to develop according to their requirements. A lenient
    /// interpretation would equate "changeable" with "removal allowed" thereby giving a System and/or
    /// planning Service freedom to remove any changeable Actions from the constraining plan in order to
    /// optimize a new *Plan for new and/or unchangeable Actions. Those removed Actions would then be
    /// dealt with in subsequent planning steps/iterations. With this definition, an "unchangeable"
    /// Action item is "System/vehicle constrained" and therefore the new *Plan being developed should
    /// avoid changes that would cause the item to be removed. A stricter interpretation might
    /// additionally require that any temporal constraints of an unchangeable Action from the
